<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TURKU, Finland 1997-04-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the the ice</p>
<p>hockey world championship on Saturday:</p>
<p>Pool B</p>
<p>Canada 7 Norway 0 (3-0 3-0 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Rob Errey (10:18), Geoff Sanderson (10:57, 14:16),</p>
<p>Owen Nolan (23:05), Keith Primeau (24:11), Anson Carter (24:59),</p>
<p>Rob Zamuner (33:46)</p>
<p>Penalties: Canada 18 minutes, Norway 10</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,800</p>
<p>Played in Helsinki</p>
<p>Pool A:</p>
<p>Czech Republic 2 Germany 1 (0-0 0-1 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Czech Republic - Martin Prochazka (45:33), Roman Simicek (56:07).</p>
<p>Germany - Mirko Ludemann (31:02).</p>
<p>Penalties: Czech Republic 6 minutes, Germany 10 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 12,862.  </p>
<p>Pool B</p>
<p>Sweden 5 Italy 3 (1-1 3-2 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Sweden - Jorgen Jonsson (12:17, 58:23), Marcus Ragnarsson (22:43), Michael Nylander (29:09), Niklas Sundblad (30:13)</p>
<p>Italy - Mario Chittaroni (15:35), Gaetano Orlando (23:33, 36:28)</p>
<p>Penalties: Sweden 14 minutes, Italy 14</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,390  </p>
<p>Pool A:</p>
<p>Finland 6 France 1 (2-0 2-1 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Finland - Mika Stromberg (01:54), Olli Jokinen (17:21, 35:30), Kai Nurminen (25:24, 52:39), Petri Varis (51:49).</p>
<p>France - Roger Dube (37:12)</p>
<p>Penalties: Finland 10 minutes, France 16 minutes. Attendance: 13,093.</p>
</text>
